language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn6le18ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Future", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can talk about the future in different ways.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"italic\">going to (+ base verb)</span>, the <span class=\"italic\">present continuous (be + -ing)</span> or <span class=\"italic\">will (+ base verb)</span>. <br><br>  The structure you use depends on what you want to say. <br><br>  You use <span class=\"italic\">will</span> to talk about things that are not decided or when you make a decision at the moment of speaking for the future. <br> <span class=\"strong\">Example</span>: <br> <span class=\"italic\">I'll help.</span> <br><br>  You use <span class=\"italic\">going to</span> to talk about intentions.<br> <span class=\"strong\">Examples:</span> <br> <span class=\"italic\">Are we going to open our gifts? <br> I'm going to have to rest a bit before I eat any more.</span>  <br><br>  The <span class=\"italic\">Present Continuous</span> tense is used to talk about things that are arranged, on the agenda or booked for the future. <br> <span class=\"strong\">Examples:</span>  <br> <span class=\"italic\">We're having our yearly family gathering tonight.</span>  <br><br>  You use the <span class=\"italic\">Simple Present</span> tense to talk about schedules or timetables in the future. <br> <span class=\"strong\">Example:</span> <br> <span class=\"italic\">The restaurant closes for 2 days at Christmas.</span> ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Saying What is Necessary", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you say what is necessary to follow advice, you use <span class=\"italic\">have got to</span>, or <span class=\"italic\">going to have to</span>.</br> <span class=\"italic\">Have got to</span> focuses on now and in the future. <span class=\"italic\">I'm going to have to</span> focuses on the future alone. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "I'm going to have to rest a bit before I eat any more.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You have to work tomorrow?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'm going to have to hide them!", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "timewise", "type": "name"}, {"content": "with respect to time", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Britain is 5 hours ahead timewise. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le18ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear at Christmas dinner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "yearly", "type": "name"}, {"content": "every  year ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We're having our yearly family gathering tonight. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le18ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to envy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to want what others have", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Everyone will envy me! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le18ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to chat ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to talk", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I always chat with my family on Christmas morning. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le18ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{